Note: jam(Sequence, Symbol, Int, String, Int, Int) chord-aware Markov + the
Note: composer-overridable Flow-file style packs at
Note:   flow-lang/improv/styles/*.flow         (shipped — jazz / blues / classical)
Note:   ~/.config/flow/styles/*.flow           (user-supplied; overrides shipped)
Note: Pack discovery + load order is owned by StyleRegistry.cs; this file just
Note: forward-declares the surface so `use "@improv"` makes the names visible.

Note: Pull in @std so (dict ...) etc. are resolvable when composer style packs
Note: `use "@improv"` and start constructing their rule packs.
use "@std"

Note: ===== Style pack registry =====

Note: (registerStyle #name (dict ...)) — mutates ExecutionContext.StyleRegistry.
Note: Last-write-wins per Pitfall 8; user packs at ~/.config/flow/styles/
Note: override shipped packs on Symbol-name collision and emit a one-shot
Note: stderr advisory.
Note: The value side uses Dict<Void, Void> as a wildcard (D-36-02-04 convention,
Note: same shape as the @std (get)/(set)/(each) Dict-side ops) so the composer
Note: can pass ANY Dict<Symbol, T> without forcing a specific generic
Note: instantiation at the call site — pack values are heterogeneous (Dict,
Note: Tuple, Dict-of-Symbol) and there is no concrete Flow type that covers
Note: all three.
internal proc registerStyle (Symbol: name, Dict<Void, Void>: pack)

Note: (listStyles) — returns Array[Symbol] of registered style names in
Note: insertion order. Composers call this to audit which packs loaded.
internal proc listStyles ()

Note: ===== Headline composer-facing API (IMPROV-01) =====

Note: jam(over=chords) chord-aware Markov improvisation per D-36-10.
Note: Only `over` is required; defaults: style=#jazz, length=8, key=null (uses
Note: active musical-context key), seed=null (PrngRegistry-routed), order=2.
Note:
Note: The String? key= argument pushes a synthetic MusicalContext frame for
Note: the jam evaluation when non-null (popped after). Use it for chromatic
Note: pivot bars that break the surrounding key context.
Note:
Note: Unseeded jam routes its PRNG through ExecutionContext.PrngRegistry keyed
Note: by (CurrentCallSite, "jam") — two consecutive renders of the same source
Note: at the same git SHA produce byte-identical output (Phase 18/25/27/28/29/33
Note: two-run cmp-clean determinism inherited via D-v1.5-06 / D-36-09).
internal proc jam (Sequence: over, Symbol: style, Int: length, String: key, Int: seed, Int: order)
internal proc jam (Sequence: over, Symbol: style, Int: length, String: key, Int: seed)
internal proc jam (Sequence: over, Symbol: style, Int: length, String: key)
internal proc jam (Sequence: over, Symbol: style, Int: length)
internal proc jam (Sequence: over, Symbol: style)
internal proc jam (Sequence: over)
